I've never been in the situation of having enough scrolls (or enough
inclination--once you're past about AC -25 or -30, additional AC isn't
worth the time to me) to do that, but it's an interesting point.

All said, though, +3 still seems to me like the better wishing point;
if you have the resources to be draining/maxing things out, you're
already at the point of having plenty of AC and it's basically just a
game at that point.  Earlier on when you're wishing things up, your AC
is likely not in the "high enough that the marginal value of a single
point is extremely low" range, and so going for the highest expected
return seems prudent.

But given your analysis, it certainly becomes something on which
reasonable minds can differ.



